  <prompt>
    Implement **Rung 5** of the Association Engine: an LLM-backed extract+classify rung. Author a NEW JPS (JSON Prompt Schema) Action that, given the normalized message envelope, produces structured output — a `$choices`-constrained set of candidate record types plus `category`, `urgency`, `obligations[]`, and `suggested actions[]` — and run it via `AppOnlyAnalysisService` (app-only / managed identity; NOT OBO). It fires only when deterministic rungs 0–3 AND semantic rung 4 fail to yield a confident association.

    Rung 5 emits **`Suggested`/`Ambiguous` ONLY, with rationale** — it NEVER auto-files (FR-11 + owner override: only deterministic rungs 0–3 ≥0.85 auto-file; AI rungs always suggest). The LLM rationale is written into `sprk_associationprovenance` so the W4 review surface (task 042) shows the reviewer why. AI may FLAG privilege but never DECIDE it (ADR-015).

    Requirements (FR-15):
    - Use the `jps-action-create` skill to author the Action JSON (instruction, `$choices`-constrained record-type output field, `category`/`urgency`/`obligations[]`/`suggestedActions[]` output fields, scopes, template params, examples). Validate with `jps-validate` before wiring.
    - Run the Action via `AppOnlyAnalysisService` (app-only/MI runtime) — reuse `AppOnlyAnalysisService.AnalyzeEmailAsync` (or the nearest existing entry) rather than building a new analysis runner. Consume via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` — do NOT inject AI-internal types into Communication code (ADR-013).
    - Enforce ADR-016 budget + ADR-014 cache; fire ONLY on rung-0–4 miss/ambiguity (NFR-05). Expose per-rung telemetry hooks for task 032.
    - Map the classification output → engine matches: candidate record types → `Suggested` associations (targets per ADR-024, org → `sprk_organization`); category/urgency/obligations feed downstream W5 Responsive Intelligence (task 053 "Communication Triage" reuses this Action's output — hence the `blocks 053`).
    - Component Justification §11: this is a NEW JPS Action (justified — no existing Action extracts+classifies communications for association); but it MUST reuse the existing `AppOnlyAnalysisService` runtime, not a new one. Answer the three-question template in the PR.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF + AI engineer authoritative on JPS Action authoring (`jps-action-create`/`jps-validate`), `AppOnlyAnalysisService` (app-only/MI analysis), ADR-013 (PublicContracts facade), ADR-016/014 (budget/cache), ADR-015 (privilege flag-only), ADR-024 (regarding), and the `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist. Aware that `Services/Ai` internals are sole-owned by `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A validated JPS extract+classify Action runs via `AppOnlyAnalysisService` as rung 5, firing only after rungs 0–4 miss/are ambiguous, producing `$choices`-constrained record-type candidates + category/urgency/obligations/suggestedActions with rationale. Rung 5 emits `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` only (never auto-files), writes rationale to provenance, flags (never decides) privilege. Consumes AI via PublicContracts; reuses `AppOnlyAnalysisService`. Build + tests green; publish-size delta + CVE reported; Placement Justification + `/conflict-check` (with r2-core coordination) in PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Rung 5 is the deepest, most expensive rung — the last resort after deterministic rungs 0–3 (W1) and semantic rung 4 (task 030). The deterministic-first ladder (NFR-05) exists precisely so this LLM rung rarely fires. Its structured output does double duty: (a) as association suggestions here, and (b) as the substrate for W5's "Communication Triage" (task 053 reuses category/urgency/obligations/suggestedActions via `DeliverComposite`) — which is why this task blocks 053.

      `AppOnlyAnalysisService.AnalyzeEmailAsync` already runs JPS Actions in the app-only/MI runtime for inbound email analysis (spec §Existing Patterns). Reuse it; do not build a parallel runner. Consume through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` — `Services/Ai` internals are sole-owned by `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2`; coordinate via `/conflict-check` and escalate if a needed seam is missing (do not fork internals).

      Auto-file boundary (FR-11): rung 5 output is ALWAYS `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` regardless of model confidence. Privilege is flagged as signal only (ADR-015) — never a filing decision.
    </background>
